# NeurIPS proceedings mirror: refuses TCP connections from GitHub-hosted
# runners ("Connection refused", not 404 -- the page itself is fine in a
# browser). Excluded because CI cannot reach the host, NOT because the
# citation is unverified: reference [6] also carries an arXiv link, which is
# still checked here, so the paper stays independently confirmable by CI.
papers.nips.cc

# W12 neuroscience citation mirrors: secondary "opened PDF" / catalog links
# for citations that are independently confirmed by a DOI or publisher record
# also present in the same doc (docs/brain-research-v3/research/neuro/
# verification-log.md carries each one's VERIFIED/PARTLY status and what was
# checked). Excluded because these specific mirrors are dead or bot-gated,
# NOT because the citation itself is unverified.
http://ilpubs.stanford.edu:8090/422/1/1999-66.pdf
https://act-r.psy.cmu.edu/actr7.x/reference-manual.pdf
https://edwp.educ.msu.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/29/2020/06/Bradley_1994_MeasuringEmotionTheSelfassessment.pdf
https://emotion.wisc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/1353/2021/11/Gross-1998-The-Emerging-Field-of-Emotion-Regulation-An-Integrative-Review.pdf
https://princetonuniversity.github.io/NEU-PSY-502/_static/pdf/Class%208/Aston-Jones2005.pdf
https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/cognitive-theory-of-consciousness/
https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038/nature07538/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07538_MOESM306_ESM.pdf
https://archive.org/details/organizationofbe00hebb
# exclude-file entries are regex: '?' is escaped so it matches the literal
# query-string separator instead of "preceding char is optional"
https://books\.google\.com/books\?id=Qb3HAAAAIAAJ
https://books\.google\.com/books\?id=VbZ9AAAAMAAJ
https://citeseerx\.ist\.psu\.edu/document\?doi=426f49ec0ab1b2f119f12436a2be619f9d53ee9f&repid=rep1&type=pdf
https://laplab.ucsd.edu/articles/Cepeda%20et%20al%202008_psychsci.pdf
